> I keep accedently bumping newts or grid bugs and killing them.  So I
> started weilding nothing to do less damage when I accedently hit, but
> I've still killed a newt that way.  Passafist in nethack is only not
> killing monsters, right?  (I mean, can you stay passifist if you hit but
> don't kill?)
Yes, you learn another trick here. Never use the motion keys without
prefixing
it with a 'g'. This way you will not hit a monster. And you may move
many spaces
at once. And you will also learn to be careful. The point is not to be
pacifist as
in you didn't kill anything. The point is to be so careful that you
don't hit anything.

This is very useful in normal games because you will avoid waking
up creatures that are sleeping and you will not hit the dreaded
floating eyes.
Nowadays I don't make that mistake anymore.

> I was thinking disarming traps gave exp but I did it and no exp, so what
> gives exp besides killing monsters? (I know I've seen something telling
> about this before, but while I'm asking passafist questions I might as
> well ask this).
No disarming traps doesn't give exp. You could get experience by eating
tripe rations,
which gives exactly 1 experience point. Or you could take a
consultation with the Oracle.
Take a major one first and a minor one next, to get an increase of 2
XL, from 1 to 3.
But we are not wanting to play a real pacifist game. Just gaining
practice. A real game
is much more difficult, and requires a lot of patience and skill.

The most important things that you learn are
1) using Pets effectively.
2) running away. This you will learn when you have to live without a
pet.
3) avoiding avoidable fights. The important thing is to explore the
whole, level and not to get into unnecessary fights, while doing so. If
some monster has a good armour then it would be useful to kill it, but
your pet will probably do that for you anyway.
4) the benefits of not leveling up. Nowadays I get paranoid if I
achieve level 7 without finishing
Minetown and Sokoban.
5) Not fighting some monsters in melee when that would be a dangerous
thing to do. Useful when you meet mind-flayers. Mind-flayers are not
that dangerous when you know how to deal with them. Nowadays I don't
genocide them.

